| sha256 | YES (forgery) | 104.5 us |
| blake3 | no | 0.8 us |


Takeaway: a naive `tag = H(secret || message)` MAC is forgeable for any Merkle-Damgard hash including SHA-256. BLAKE3's tree construction (plus its dedicated keyed_hash mode) makes the same attack fail by construction. Bitcoin's use of H(H(x)) for block / tx ids does not rely on the secret-prefix MAC pattern, so this demo is about general construction safety, not a Bitcoin vulnerability.
